# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file when possible.

The format is based on Keep a Changelog:
https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/

## [Unreleased]

## [1.3.3] - 2026-11-13

### Changed
- Built the LJ examples from callable radial masks applied with NumPy's
  existing add_sphere/add_spheres operations. Negative values subtract masks.
- Moved exact, chunked sphere geometry into a generic iterator shared by the
  mask primitive and the retained LJ construction wrapper.
- Removed full contribution and candidate energy grids from iterative Ar MC;
  rejected deletions restore saved local voxel values exactly.

### Validation
- Added generic Gaussian-mask, temporary-memory, rollback, and allocation tests.
- Repeated the 3000-step drift audit using the primitive-based MC example.

## [1.3.2] - 2026-11-13

### Documentation
- Expanded sidebar navigation depth so advanced example pages and their
  sections remain visible under Examples, with the current page highlighted.
- Included custom sidebar templates in source distributions.

## [1.3.1] - 2026-11-13

### Documentation
- Grouped the LJ insertion-bias and iterative Ar MC guides under advanced
  sampling examples, after the existing feature examples and benchmarks.
- Labelled each drift-axis tick with its exponent and added the maximum error
  to the plot title.
- Documented the reservoir activity, chemical potential, fugacity, and explicit
  insertion/deletion acceptance rules; added interacting detailed-balance tests.

## [1.3.0] - 2026-11-13

### Added
- Optional pairwise energy caps and cutoff energy shifts, with a shared public
  LJ pair evaluator for continuous and grid energies.
- An empty-box Ar GCMC example with incremental grid updates, drift audits
  against full regeneration, and fixed-configuration cutoff comparisons.

## [1.2.0] - 2026-11-13

### Added
- Support for triclinic LJ insertion grids using atom-centered cutoff spheres,
  reciprocal-vector bounds, and explicit periodic-image accumulation.
- A reproducible continuous-position insertion-sampling benchmark and documented
  variance-reduction results, with proposal-density corrections and setup costs.

## [1.1.0] - 2026-11-13

### Added
- UFF van der Waals parameters for 31 elements, converted to sigma in Angstrom
  and epsilon in eV, with geometric UFF or Lorentz-Berthelot mixing.
- Chunked single-atom LJ insertion-energy grids for orthogonal periodic cells,
  evaluating actual atom-to-voxel-center distances with a minimum-image cutoff.
- Stable normalized insertion probabilities with a uniform proposal component.
- An offline Ar/carbon-cage example with optional ASE structure input, slice
  plots, NPZ export, and continuous proposals with their probability densities.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-08-10

### Added
- Added broader probe-accessibility validation against PoreBlazer-style
  calculations across multiple zeolite and MOF systems.
- Added the experimental CuPy backend to the mask-generation benchmark and
  expanded the benchmark systems to roughly 6000 atoms with checkpointed CSV
  output.

### Changed
- Expanded the documentation and benchmark figures for the multi-framework
  validation and backend comparisons.
- Build pure-Python release wheels by default; compiling the optional C++
  backend now requires ``ATOMVOXELIZER_BUILD_CPP=1``.

## [0.7.0] - 2026-07-26

### Changed
- Refactored field-grid operations and plotting to reuse the base voxel-grid
  indexing and voxel-center geometry helpers.

## [0.6.1] - 2026-07-26

### Added
- Added an opt-in ``VoxelGridNumba.add_spheres_cell_colored`` path for
  constant-mask sphere addition using a 27-color spatial-cell schedule and
  Numba CPU parallelism.
- Added Numba cell-coloring prepared-plan helpers and tests covering mixed
  radii and prepared updates.
- Added a Numba cell-coloring benchmark with system-scaling and thread-scaling
  modes, plus documentation figures for the main examples benchmark.

### Changed
- Updated the main mask-generation benchmark figure to include the opt-in Numba
  27-color path while keeping the GPU benchmark separate.

## [0.6.0] - 2026-07-26

### Added
- Added a voxel-guided CO adsorption/desorption MCMD nanoparticle example using
  ORB-V3 CPU by default.
- Added an experimental CuPy 27-color cell-coloring sphere-add path for
  GPU-resident constant masks, including mixed-radius batches by coloring with
  the largest radius and grouping updates by radius.
- Added a focused GPU benchmark comparing CPU Numba, the existing CuPy
  ``add.at`` path, the CuPy 27-color kernel, a prepared CuPy 27-color plan, and
  high-level Torch prototypes on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090.

### Changed
- Renamed the previous Wulff nanoparticle MC example to
  ``examples/mc/orb_v3_co_mcmd.py`` and updated the quickstart around MCMD
  coverage control.
- Reworked ``benchmarks/benchmark_backends.py`` into a CPU mask-generation
  benchmark comparing a direct atom-grid distance scan with ``VoxelGrid`` NumPy
  and ``VoxelGridNumba`` across zeolite, nanoparticle, and surface workloads up
  to roughly 3000 atoms.
- Improved the CO MCMD example by using a larger finite-cell padding, the
  ORB-V3 infinite-neighbor model by default, clean-nanoparticle optimization,
  CO-only insertion optimization, refreshed voxel adsorption sites each MC
  cycle, broader sampling over all non-core surface site types, a
  surface-atom-based maximum CO coverage, and clamped chemical-potential
  feedback.

### Fixed
- Fixed the CO MCMD example so sampled voxel-site counts cannot let CO loading
  exceed the requested maximum coverage relative to nanoparticle surface atoms.

## [0.2.13] - 2026-07-03

### Added
- Expanded pytest coverage for NumPy voxel-grid arithmetic, plotting helpers,
  analysis edge cases, lazy imports, vector-field plotting, and Numba backend
  equivalence.

### Fixed
- Matched Numba distance-mask division behavior to NumPy for zero-distance
  center voxels in real-valued grids.

## [0.2.12] - 2026-07-03

### Changed
- Changed the voxel-guided MC example temperature to Kelvin and converted
  Metropolis sampling internally with ``kB*T``.
- Changed MC trial-site selection to prefer voxel sites local to the selected
  atom, avoiding strained global trial directions.
- Added command-line controls for the MC shell/core mask multipliers, sampled
  count range, maximum sampled sites, and local trial-site radius.
- Updated the quickstart MC image to a 1500 K EMT run with about 20%
  acceptance and final-state displacement coloring.

## [0.2.11] - 2026-07-02

### Added
- Added GitLab CI coverage reporting with pytest-cov terminal output and a
  Cobertura ``coverage.xml`` report artifact.
- Added an ASE-rendered initial/final nanoparticle state image for the
  voxel-guided MC quickstart.
- Added ``--state-plot`` to ``examples/mc/orb_v3_wulff_mc.py``.

### Changed
- Replaced the quickstart MC geometric placeholder score with ASE EMT as the
  default scorer.
- Consolidated documentation pages into a simpler navigation structure while
  keeping lightweight compatibility pages for older documentation URLs.
- Fixed the ORB-V3 quickstart scorer so the conservative model can use
  autograd during prediction.

## [0.2.10] - 2026-07-02

### Added
- Added optional Numba backends for experimental field-valued grids:
  ``FieldVoxelGridNumba`` and ``VectorVoxelGridNumba``.
- Added ASE trajectory output for the voxel-guided MC quickstart example.
- Added probe-center accessibility analysis from supplied positions, atomic
  radii, and probe radius.
- Added sampled probe-accessible surface-area estimation for inflated atom
  surfaces.
- Added a probe pore-volume documentation page with a BEA comparison against
  PoreBlazer.

### Changed
- Clarified the algorithm documentation around cached sphere stencils and
  scaling relative to all grid-point-by-atom distance scans.
- Renamed the voxel-guided MC example folder from ``examples/mcmd`` to
  ``examples/mc`` and removed MCMD wording.
- Ignored local ``tmp/`` scratch folders so compiled comparison tools and
  generated reference outputs are not tracked.

### Fixed
- Aligned the field-grid normal-mask documentation visual with voxel centers.

## [0.2.9] - 2026-07-01

### Added
- Added an experimental NumPy-only ``FieldVoxelGrid`` for scalar, vector, and
  matrix-valued voxel fields.
- Added ``VectorVoxelGrid`` as a convenience field grid for three-component
  vector fields, including atom-normal sphere masks and Matplotlib quiver
  plotting helpers.
- Added field-grid documentation, tests, and a reproducible normal-mask visual
  example.

## [0.2.8] - 2026-06-30

### Added
- Added ``dtype`` support for voxel grids, including integer, floating, and
  complex NumPy dtypes where backend support is available.
- Added a dtype benchmark script for comparing grid storage types.
- Documented dtype behavior and performance considerations.

### Changed
- Complex grids now support arithmetic sphere operations but reject ordered
  operations such as ``min_sphere``, ``clamp_grid``, range sampling, and
  threshold plotting.

## [0.2.7] - 2026-06-29

### Added
- First public release in a documentation ready state
- Taichi, CuPy, and Numba accelerators implemented
